{"question_id": "V2-dev-RPT-en-T2-002", "approach": "B1", "approach_base": "B1", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "D", "corpus_set": "D_en", "answer_text": "Delivery Hero’s 2024 annual report treats the rider‑classification risk in Spain differently for the two business models:  \n\n1. **Model used before August 2021** – the risk is deemed “more likely than not” to materialise, so a provision is recorded in the Group’s Consolidated Financial Statements.  \n2. **Model used since August 2021** – the risk is considered possible (but not probable), so it is disclosed as a contingency in the Consolidated Financial Statements.  \n\nGlovo has decided to **progressively transition to an employment‑based model for its riders in Spain, effective 2025** to avoid further legal uncertainties.  \n\n**Points**  \n- [1] “Where it is more likely than not that a rider risk materialises… this is the case with risks in Spain in relation to the model operated by Glovo until August 2021.”  \n- [1] “Where the rider risk is deemed possible (but not probable)… this is the case with risks in relation to Glovo Spain after August 2021.”  \n- [3] “In December 2024, DH announced Glovo’s management decision to progressively move to an employment‑based model in Spain to avoid further legal uncertainties in relation to the model in place since August 2021.”", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 727 chars]", "doc_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en", "section_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::h201", "unit_ids": ["D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::p128_b9"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 0, "span": [466060, 466787], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 788 chars]", "doc_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en", "section_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::h320", "unit_ids": ["D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::p204_b14"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 1, "span": [709497, 710285], "meta